---
title: HTTP API Reference
description: Every REST/OIDC route, with request/response shapes and auth requirements.
---

Base URL: `ISSUER_URL` (e.g. `https://auth.neoworks.dev`).

Auth columns:
- **None** — no authentication required.
- **Bearer** — `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` (validated by
  `middleware.JWTMiddleware`: signature + expiry check, then a Redis
  revocation-list lookup).
- **Cookie** — browser session cookie set by the login/consent flow.

For the end-to-end authorization code flow, see [oauth](/docs/api/oauth).

---

## OIDC discovery & keys

| Method | Path | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/.well-known/openid-configuration` | None | Static OIDC discovery document (issuer, endpoints, supported grants/PKCE methods) |
| GET | `/.well-known/jwks.json` | None | Public JWKS for verifying access tokens (ES256), cached 1h |

---

## OAuth2 / OIDC core endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/oauth/authorize` | None | Authorization endpoint. See [oauth](/docs/api/oauth#1-authorize) |
| POST | `/oauth/token` | None (client creds in form/body) | Token endpoint — `authorization_code` and `refresh_token` grants. See [oauth](/docs/api/oauth#3-token-exchange) |
| POST | `/oauth/introspect` | None (form) | RFC 7662 token introspection |
| POST | `/oauth/revoke` | None (form) | RFC 7009 token revocation (always 200) |
| GET | `/oauth/userinfo` | Bearer | OIDC UserInfo — returns `sub`, and `email` if the `email` scope was granted |

### `GET /oauth/authorize`

Query params: `client_id`, `redirect_uri`, `response_type=code`, `scope`
(space-separated), `state`, `code_challenge`, `code_challenge_method=S256`.

Validates the client exists, `redirect_uri` is registered, scopes are
allowed, and PKCE params are present with `S256` (plain rejected). On
success, redirects (302) to `/auth/login?login_challenge={id}`.

### `POST /oauth/token`

Form-encoded body.

**`grant_type=authorization_code`**
| Field | Required |
|---|---|
| `code` | yes |
| `redirect_uri` | yes (must match the one used at `/oauth/authorize`) |
| `code_verifier` | yes (`base64url(SHA256(code_verifier)) == code_challenge`) |

**`grant_type=refresh_token`**
| Field | Required |
|---|---|
| `refresh_token` | yes (the refresh token JTI) |

Response:

```json
{
  "access_token": "<JWT>",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 900,
  "refresh_token": "<jti>",
  "scope": "openid profile email"
}
```

- Access tokens are valid for **15 minutes**, refresh tokens for **30 days**.
- Refresh is **rotating**: the old refresh token is atomically marked
  `used` and a new pair is issued. Reusing an already-used/revoked refresh
  token revokes the entire grant (replay protection), guarded by a
  short-lived Redis lock per JTI.

### `POST /oauth/introspect`

Form body: `token`. Response:

```json
{ "active": true, "sub": "...", "client_id": "...", "scope": "...", "exp": 0, "iat": 0, "iss": "...", "jti": "...", "token_type": "Bearer" }
```
or `{ "active": false }` if invalid/expired/revoked.

### `POST /oauth/revoke`

Form body: `token`, optional `token_type_hint` (`access_token` |
`refresh_token`). Always responds `200 OK`. Revoking a refresh token also
revokes its grant if the token was already used.

### `GET /oauth/userinfo`

Requires Bearer token. Response:

```json
{ "sub": "<user_id>", "email": "user@example.com" }
```
(`email` only present if the access token's scopes include `email`.)

---

## Login / signup / consent (browser flow)

These render server-side HTML and are driven by the SvelteKit frontend via
redirects. See [oauth](/docs/api/oauth) for the full sequence.

| Method | Path | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/auth/login` | None | Login form. `?login_challenge=` required. Auto-advances if a valid `sso_session` cookie exists. |
| POST | `/auth/login` | None | Form: `email`, `password`, `login_challenge`. On success sets `sso_session` cookie (30 days, HttpOnly, Secure) and proceeds to `/oauth/callback/login`. |
| GET | `/auth/signup` | None | Signup form. `?login_challenge=` required. |
| POST | `/auth/signup` | None | Form: `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `password` (≥8 chars), `login_challenge`. Creates the user, then proceeds like login. |
| GET | `/oauth/consent` | Cookie (`login_session`, 10 min) | Consent screen with human-readable scope descriptions. Auto-skipped if the user already granted the requested scopes (or `auto_grant_scopes` is set on the client). |
| POST | `/oauth/consent` | Cookie (`login_session`) | Form: `login_challenge`, `action` (`allow` to accept), `scopes[]` (deselect individual scopes). Persists a `grant` and redirects back to the client. |

Scope labels shown on the consent screen: `openid` → "Verify identity",
`profile` → "Access profile", `email` → "Access email", `offline` → "Stay
signed in".

---

## Internal callback endpoints (SvelteKit → server)

| Method | Path | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/oauth/callback/login` | None | Body: `{ "login_challenge", "user_id" }`. Returns `{ "redirect": ... }` — either straight to the client (`?code=...&state=...`) if scopes are already granted, or to `/oauth/consent?consent_challenge=...`. |
| POST | `/oauth/callback/consent` | None | Body: `{ "consent_challenge", "accepted", "scopes": [...] }`. Returns `{ "redirect": ... }` to the client with `?code=...&state=...` (accepted) or `?error=access_denied` (denied). |

---

## End-to-end key & device management (`handlers/keys`)

Used by the client-side encryption model (Account Master Key wrapped per
password / recovery key / device — see [architecture](/docs/api/architecture#identity--encryption-model)).

### Public

| Method | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/auth/key-challenge?email=` | Returns the user's `password_wrapped_amk`, Argon2 KDF params (`argon2_salt`, `argon2_time`, `argon2_memory`, `argon2_threads`, `argon2_keylen`) so the client can derive the password key and unwrap the AMK locally. |
| POST | `/api/v1/keys/device-invite` | Body: `{ "device_public_key" }`. Returns `{ "token" }` — a short-lived (10 min) invite for a new device to be approved via QR code. |
| GET | `/api/v1/keys/device-invite/{token}` | `202 Accepted` while pending; once approved, `200` with `{ "wrapped_amk" }` (1h TTL on the result). |

### Authenticated (Bearer)

| Method | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/v1/keys` | Initial key setup: recovery-wrapped AMK, password-wrapped AMK + Argon2 params, and the first device's public key + wrapped AMK. `204 No Content`. |
| POST | `/api/v1/keys/devices` | Body: `{ "public_key", "wrapped_amk", "name" }`. Registers a new device, returns the device record. |
| GET | `/api/v1/keys/devices` | Lists the caller's registered devices. |
| GET | `/api/v1/keys/devices/me?public_key=` | Returns `{ "wrapped_amk" }` for the caller's device matching `public_key`, or `404` if not registered. Used by a returning browser to unwrap its AMK with its locally-stored device private key. |
| GET | `/api/v1/keys/recovery` | Returns `{ "recovery_wrapped_amk" }`. |
| PUT | `/api/v1/keys/recovery` | Body: `{ "recovery_wrapped_amk" }`. Rotates the recovery wrapping. `204 No Content`. |
| POST | `/api/v1/keys/device-invite/{token}/approve` | Body: `{ "wrapped_amk", "device_name" }`. An existing device approves a pending invite, completing the new device's setup. `204 No Content`. |

---

## Media (`handlers/media`) — all Bearer-authenticated

Encrypted, content-addressed, deduplicated (per-user) chunked file storage
on top of MinIO/S3.

| Method | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/v1/media/check` | Body: `{ "chunks": [{ "hash", "size" }, ...] }`. Returns `{ "missing_chunks": [...] }` so the client only uploads chunks the server doesn't already have. |
| PUT | `/api/v1/media/chunks/{hash}` | Body: raw encrypted bytes (≤16 MiB). SHA-256 of body must equal `{hash}`. `201` (new) or `200` (already exists). |
| GET | `/api/v1/media/chunks/{hash}` | Streams the raw encrypted chunk (`application/octet-stream`). |
| POST | `/api/v1/media` | Body: `{ "filename", "mime_type", "chunks": [{ "hash", "size" }, ...] }`. Finalizes a new media object from previously-uploaded chunks. `201` with the media record. |
| PUT | `/api/v1/media/{id}` | Body: `{ "parent_version_id", ...optional filename/mime_type/chunks }`. Creates a new version of an existing media item. |
| GET | `/api/v1/media` | Query: `limit` (default 50, max 200), `offset`. Lists the caller's media (metadata only). |
| GET | `/api/v1/media/{id}` | Returns full metadata for one media item. |
| DELETE | `/api/v1/media/{id}` | `204 No Content`. Deletes the media record and garbage-collects any chunks whose `ref_count` drops to 0 (removing the S3 blob). |

Storage accounting: `user.storage_used_bytes` is updated on chunk
create/delete; `chunk.ref_count` tracks references across
`media.chunks` + `media_version.chunks` for GC. See
[data model](/docs/api/data-model).
